==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Poultrio]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**3 [[Darkmadillo]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage introduces Poultrio, who is like M. Ost but on even more crack. Compared to other R. Ost variants, Poultrio has an insanely fast speed and attack time alongside an Omni-Strike, and the high DPS as expected from other R. Ost variants, meaning that Poultrio is extremely difficult to stall. Traditional meatshield options like Manic Eraser or specialist meatshields like Jetpack, Maize, or Carpenter will die immediately due to Poultrio's ridiculously high DPS and range combined with rapid-fire Explosions that Knockback, and even Rock isn't enough given that Rock will activate Poultrio's Omni-Strike, damaging your other units. As a result, even with almost no support like with this stage, Poultrio is a menace which you need to dedicate the majority of your lineup towards countering. Crowd-Control is also almost completely useless against Poultrio thanks to its Aku Shield and twenty Knockbacks, as well as how hard sneaking in squishy traditional CCers is thanks to Poultrio's effective range, although you still will want Crowd-Control because fighting Poultrio without any way to restrain it will lead towards someone dying, and it won't be Poultrio who does. Because of this, the most consistent way to counter Poultrio is to use an inconsistent class of units: meatshields with [[Dodge Attack]] against Poultrio's three traits. While Dodge meatshields will be expensive to spam, especially because you'll want two or three to be fully safe, a common theme you'll notice within Poultrio's four stages is that you'll always have cash supply enemies, though they don't really spawn quick enough for you to be fully covered throughout the whole battle, as you'll want plenty of heavy units, whether they be Mythics units like Uril and Mewtone, or just Ubers.

For this stage in particular, you have a bunch of cash supplies in the form of Celeboodle and Doge Dark, Darkmadillos that don't really do anything given that Poultrio is already jumping every unit you spawn, and Poultrio itself. Try to be cautious and stall the initial Celeboodle, as using a Can Can or whatever unit can lead towards your unit prematurely launching the Poultrio towards your base without enough money to properly fight it head-on. Once you're ready, lure Poultrio and then kill it as fast as you can. This way, all the supporting enemies and cash supplies will die or get damage knockbacks before they can actually interfere too much.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*Dodge meatshields: You will need Dodge meatshields to even stand a chance against Poultrio's extremely rapid and powerful attacks. Examples include [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]], [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mohawk Cat]], Talented [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Flying Ninja Cat]], and a Talented [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]]. For this stage specifically, you can get away with just one in either Bellydance, Bondage, or Flying Ninja Cat paired with Boulder and Jetpack Cat. You will want to boost whichever one you end up going with. But if you want to beat the other three stages, you'll ideally want at least two Dodge meatshields at a time. Bondage Cat is the recommended pick over Flying Ninja Cat due to having actually decent base HP.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Rock is required to bring along on its stage due to its blazing fast speed and recharge and powerful stalling potential, making it extremely helpful to  stall Poultrio. Also pretty good at baiting out Celeboodle and Doge Dark hits given that both units are Single Target enemies with high damage. Use Boulder carefully, as if you waste a Boulder by allowing Poultrio to hit both it and a Dodge meatshield, Poultrio can eventually kill the Dodge meatshield then gain immense amounts of ground while your next Boulder is still on its cooldown.
*[[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Crystal Li'l Gau Gau]]: Li'l Gau on this stage is extremely good even given its lack of Dodge, having an extremely fast cooldown, Knockback Immune, and great effective health against Poultrio. Can also tank a Doge Dark hit, if things come to that.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train is very useful on these stages if luck is on your side. Depending on how many times Poultrio decides to launch Knockbacks, it can land a bunch of extra damage and brute force the Shield. It also works well in sniping the Doge Darks and Celeboodles for quick cash injections as well as potentially being able to land a big hit on Darkmadillo.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Poultrio pushes crazy hard, meaning that Cyberpunk and Deadeye are welcome additions here alongside your Legend Cats. However, Cyberpunk's massive blind spot means that even with his Survive Talent, it is incredibly easy for him to become a waste of a slot if Poultrio is able to push even a little bit into your units. If you're using these two units, try not to lure too hard as you don't want your Deadeye or Cyberpunk to get spawncamped by Poultrio's Explosion
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]]: Doron doesn't target any enemy on this stage, but his huge damage and Surge allows him to get some very important cheap damage onto the enemies here, especially Darkmadillo. It might also be useful to remember that Doron has a crazy amount of health, meaning if you really need to, you can use him as a tank for a few seconds.
*[[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Mewtone]]: Mewtone is an immeasurably powerful super-backliner whose long Slow vs. Red helps out considerably against the boss, and Mewtone's high damage makes him perfect to chip down the other enemies. His Conjure is also a nice option to push off a Celeboodle or Doge Dark.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]: Uril and his True Form are practically required for this stage with his powerful anti-Aku crowd-control, which can disable Poultrio's extremely annoying Knockback and Slow him very well.
*[[Giga-Nyan Rex (Uber Rare Cat)|Giga-Nyan Rex]]: Giga-Nyan Rex is really bad most of the time, but given Poultrio's properties Giga-Nyan Rex can actually be useful if you don't have anything else to run. Its short Slow can combo well with Uril and Mewtone, Strong vs. Dark, and most importantly Explosion Immunity makes it a decent generalist to use. Think of Giga-Nyan Rex like using Heroic Musashi on Floor 30: a bad unit with poor stats who has to stand in the back for the boss and slowly chip the enemies down.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Thundia β]]: Thundia lacks immunities to Poultrio, but her massive nuke damage to Poultrio allows her to ignore those issues. With a multi-hit which can both brute-force the Shield and get a damage knockback onto Poultrio, using Thundia you can get a quick clear of the stage. As a bonus, her second hit's range can also allow her to work to get huge damage off onto Darkmadillo. What puts Thundia over the edge compared to almost every other Uber option for this stage, however, is her being able to abuse Poultrio's Knockbacks to the fullest: often, Thundia will get her first, more damaging hit off on Poultrio, thus either landing a damage knockback or brute-forcing its Shield, then get knocked back by Poultrio, thus allowing her to start her attack again.
*Ultra Talented [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: With her Target Aku and Defense Buff Talents, Kai is able to wall the boss immensely, and her high damage and Shield Piercing Talent can also get a decent chunk out onto the boss. Just make sure she doesn't take much damage from Celeboodle or Doge Dark, as they'll quickly tear through Kai's health.
*[[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Phantasmal Nobunaga]]: A single Phantasmal Nobunaga hit onto an unshielded Poultrio can cripple Poultrio for a huge amount of time, and alongside other DPS options to constantly break Poultrio's Shield you can get a huge amount of damage off. Similarly, [[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Crystal Cat]] also has a lengthy Freeze, although with a shorter foreswing and a shorter Freeze. If you have Ice Cat's Ultra Talents for whatever reason, her Dodge Talent is a considerable help for this stage, and her Strengthen Talent can allow her to dish out a pretty good amount of damage.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: Yukimura maintains his relevance as in any other stage, being a rusher to get huge damage off onto Poultrio and then die. Thanks to Poultrio's Knockbacks, if you get lucky you can get a bunch of rebounds and deal huge damage with Yukimura.
*[[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Hellrider Kenshin]]: Kenshin's good health and double Knockback with her Mini-Wave allows her to push Poultrio to the base as well as chip away at the supporting enemies with said Mini-Wave. Be careful using her, as you can easily get Uril to miss his attack if using her.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Jizo's Mega-Castle]]: Kasa Jizo's Ultra Form is really bad for this stage, but his True Form on the other hand is a decently okay nuker here, albeit with some problems due to his multi-hit potentially creating some problems with Poultrio's Explosions and Knockbacks.
*[[The White Rabbit (Uber Rare Cat)|The Spectral Cat]]: Spectral Cat's high effective health and damage makes her a really good Uber for Poultrio, as well as having some incredibly powerful CC in the form of a lengthy Slow and crippling Weaken which can easily combo with Uril and Mewtone. As a bonus, her initial hit is able to brute-force Poultrio's Shield, and her second and third hits will then apply the Weaken and Slow onto Poultrio.
*Ultra Talented [[Anubis the Protector (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Anubis]]: If you have Anubis's Ultra Talents for whatever reason, he is a decently viable option for this stage thanks to his Knockback Immunity, chance of piercing Shields, and high DPS, alongside an unreliable Surge which can nuke a supporting enemy if it actually lands. However, given Poultrio's extremely aggressive nature, the playstyle of luring into Anubis's range to allow his attack to connect is very risky thanks to his long foreswing.
*[[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S. Beartooth]]: With its Dodge Talent, B.C.S. Beartooth becomes an incredibly powerful anti-Poultrio nuker able to deal huge amounts of damage onto Poultrio while also having Knockback Immunity and a decent chance to dodge Poultrio's attacks. The Dodge Talent in particular is what makes Beartooth so strong here, being able to withstand a bunch of Poultrio hits while dishing out crazy damage that can remove high amounts of the boss's health.
*[[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|NEK-03 Cloud Emperor]]: Bomburr's Ultra Form isn't the greatest backliner generalist to exist, but even if Untalented, Bomburr's Explosions, if they occur, can force damage knockbacks onto the supporting enemies. The main appeal of Bomburr's Ultra Form, though, is its Explosion Immunity, allowing it to stay on the field for a decent amount of time before it finally goes down.
*Ultra Talented [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]]: With her Dodge Talent, Mer-Queen Ruri acts as a big version of Bellydance, except with actual damage which can get huge value off on the supporting enemies.
*[[Adventurer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Fabled Adventurer Girl Kanna]]: Kanna is another nuker option, but a bit better compared to Pai-Pai or Eva Unit-02 due to her Surges and Long Distance, allowing her to chip away at Darkmadillo as well as more importantly deal strong amounts of damage against Poultrio.
*[[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai DX]]: Pai-Pai's foreswing is really annoying to deal with, but if the Shield has been broken beforehand, she can get a lot of damage onto Poultrio assuming Poultrio has been hit by Uril. Similarly, [[EVA Unit-02 (Uber Rare Cat)|Unit-02, Code 777]] does the same thing as Pai-Pai, being a big nuker for albeit a bit worse due to its Long Distance, foreswing, and lack of effective health against Red.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: Phonoa's ridiculous effective DPS and high range allows them to stand safely in the backline as long as your defense is good and chip away at Poultrio and the supporting enemies. To an extent, [[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] also does the same job, albeit with a bit more risk as their rather short Slow (2 secs) can override longer Slow effects, like that of Mewtone.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Lunacia's excellent crowd-control and damage to the boss makes her one of the strongest Uber options available for this Advent.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Luminous]]: Lunos isn't as great against Poultrio's stages compared to most other stages due to its Shield and really strong pushing power, but given that Lunos targets Dark, you can use him as a quick tanking option as well as for his Conjure for supporting enemy purposes. Just be careful of your cash, as you can easily go broke if there isn't a Celeboodle or Doge Dark ready to die.
*[[Hajime Saito (Uber Rare Cat)|Hajime Saito]]: Saito's blazing Speed and guaranteed Shield Piercing makes him a pretty good unit here, able to rush into Poultrio to get an extremely damaging hit off.
*[[Baki Hanma (Uber Rare Cat)|Baki Hanma]]: Baki is pretty good here with his high DPS, Explosion Immunity, short cooldown and rapid attacks allowing him to constantly Knockback Poultrio. As a bonus, Baki has a small chance to instantly Pierce Poultrio's Shield.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama]]: Hanayama is usually super impractical to use thanks to his foreswing and tendency to miss, but given you're luring these all work in Hanayama's favor, who can nuke Poultrio and get a ton of value off. Just make sure to protect him from the supporting enemies, as his base health isn't the greatest.
*Knockback-Immune Ubers: Quite a few Ubers have a Knockback Immunity Talent that often make them worse in almost every scenario possible. However, if you choose to purchase this Talent and thus make your Uber worse for the rest of the game, a lot of Ubers that previously would be deadweights thanks to Poultrio's constant Knockback and Explosion are now able to actually do a decent bit of work here. Examples include [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]], [[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]], [[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Hevijak]], and [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]].
*[[Musashi Miyamoto (Legend Rare Cat)|Immortal Miyamoto]]: You'll often find periods where there are very few enemies on screen, meaning Immortal Miyamoto can easily go to town here with his really high stats against Dark.
*[[Jeanne (Legend Rare Cat)|Divine Jeanne ψ]]: In her True Form, Jeanne gains buffs which allows her to work against Poultrio, although not fully counter it. Jeanne just so happens to stand 10 range away from Poultrio's Omni Strike and be Explosion-Immune, meaning that if you properly protect her she should theoretically be able to work as a really good Explosion-Immune nuker for the boss. However, the fact that she only outranges it by 10 means that you need to run support units like Uril, Mewtone, and have good meatshielding options to prevent her from getting destroyed by Poultrio.

